{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv returned 0xe0 (TRAP uart data mismatch, tohost FAIL 0xdead). Start state 1 waits half-bit with 2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider but states 10/default advance on recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4), 16x too short. This early sampling shifts ser_rx into recv_pattern before full bit periods elapse, corrupting recv_buf_data to 0xe0.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,14 +89,14 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
 				end
", "expected": "tohost PASS, loopback 0xa5 matched, no uart data mismatch TRAP"}

